%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: aeb7f43e27df0304d810078ac50d9265, type: 3}
  m_Name: Case_1A
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ProCommVR.Hospital.PatientCase
  _difficulty: 0
  _doorLabel: 1A
  _patientName: Mr. X
  _age: 51
  _room: 1A
  _situation: Mr. X has a leg infection that needs intravenous antibiotics for a
    few more days. Today is his granddaughter's birthday, and he refuses physical
    therapy and mobilization.
  _watchOut: Acknowledge his disappointment without making promises about his discharge.
  _patientPrefab: {fileID: 6337038501055911691, guid: e5176871290f3c54daf563c0c59a5c00, type: 3}
  _startPose: 0
  _npcLine: What's the point? I just want to stay in bed and go home.
  _options:
  - _title: Professional Empathy & Collaborative Encouragement
    _text: I completely understand how heartbreaking this is, Mr. X. Being there
      for your granddaughter's special day means the world to you. While the infection
      means we must keep you here under the doctor's care for a few more days to
      ensure you heal safely, staying active is actually what will help you get back
      on your feet faster. How about we do a short walk together today, and afterward,
      I can help you set up a video call so you can sing happy birthday to her?
    _score: 3
    _feedback: Validates emotional distress, stays strictly within nursing scope
      without making medical promises, and redirects the patient toward recovery
      and positive connection. Patient agrees to get out of bed.
  - _title: Dismissive & Rule-Bound
    _text: Mr. X, staying in bed won't fix anything. The doctor said you have an
      infection, so you simply cannot be discharged. You need to follow hospital
      protocol, get out of bed, and start moving. There will be other birthdays.
    _score: 0
    _feedback: Emotionally invalidates the patient, damages therapeutic rapport,
      and triggers resistance. Patient turns away and refuses to communicate further.
  - _title: Boundary Overstep & False Hope
    _text: 'Oh, please don''t be sad! Tell you what: let me talk to the doctor and
      see if we can just discharge you early for the afternoon. If you promise to
      rest at home, I''m sure it''ll be fine and you can make it to the party.'
    _score: -2
    _feedback: Breaches professional boundaries by undermining clinical safety and
      medical authority, providing false clinical reassurance. Leg infection risks
      severe complications.
  - _title: Passive Avoidance / Deflection
    _text: I'm sorry to hear that. Discharge decisions are entirely up to your doctor,
      so there's nothing I can really do about it. If you don't feel like getting
      up right now, I'll just leave you alone and come back later.
    _score: 1
    _feedback: Fails to motivate or comfort the patient. Leaves the patient isolated,
      risking worsening mobility and deepening depressive symptoms.
